{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QpwVfAjmxqbjF14Zomoknf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd050-readlink\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/readlink: Print Symlink Target or Canonical Path\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Scripts that manage symbolic links use readlink to inspect link targets and resolve\n6\t  symlink chains to canonical paths. readlink supports multiple canonicalization modes\n7\t  (-f, -e, -m) that differ in how they handle missing path components. The Go implementation\n8\t  must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (greadlink, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte\n9\t  on stdout and exit code, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Print the target of a symbolic link.\n13\t  - G2: Support canonicalization modes (-f, -e, -m) for resolving full paths.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Default behavior and canonicalization\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: When invoked with a symlink operand and no flags, must print the immediate target of the symbolic link followed by a newline and exit 0.\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: If the operand is not a symbolic link (with no flags), must print nothing to stdout and exit 1.\n23\t      - R1.3:\n24\t          text: \"-f (--canonicalize) must resolve the full canonical path, following all symlinks. The final component need not exist, but the directory containing it must exist.\"\n25\t      - R1.4:\n26\t          text: \"-e (--canonicalize-existing) must resolve the full canonical path. Every component of the path must exist; otherwise exit 1.\"\n27\t      - R1.5:\n28\t          text: \"-m (--canonicalize-missing) must resolve the full canonical path. No component need exist.\"\n29\t      - R1.6:\n30\t          text: \"-n (--no-newline) must suppress the trailing newline when printing a single operand.\"\n31\t\n32\t  R2:\n33\t    title: Multiple operands\n34\t    items:\n35\t      - R2.1:\n36\t          text: When multiple operands are given, must print each result on a separate line.\n37\t      - R2.2:\n38\t          text: When multiple operands are given with -n, -n is ignored (newlines are always printed between results).\n39\t\n40\t  R3:\n41\t    title: Error handling\n42\t    items:\n43\t      - R3.1:\n44\t          text: If no operand is provided, must print a usage error to stderr and exit 1.\n45\t      - R3.2:\n46\t          text: Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n47\t\n48\t  R4:\n49\t    title: Differential testing\n50\t    items:\n51\t      - R4.1:\n52\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (greadlink) via pkg/testutils.\n53\t      - R4.2:\n54\t          text: \"Tests must cover: symlink target, non-symlink operand, -f with existing and partial paths, -e with existing and missing paths, -m with missing paths, -n flag, multiple operands, and error cases.\"\n55\t      - R4.3:\n56\t          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n57\t\n58\tnon_goals:\n59\t  - cmd/readlink does not create or modify symbolic links; use cmd/ln for that.\n60\t  - cmd/readlink does not support --relative-to or --relative-base; use cmd/realpath for relative output.\n61\t\n62\tacceptance_criteria:\n63\t  - id: AC1\n64\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/readlink on a symlink prints the target, matching greadlink.\"\n65\t    traces:\n66\t      - R1.1\n67\t      - R1.2\n68\t      - R1.3\n69\t      - R1.4\n70\t      - R1.5\n71\t      - R1.6\n72\t  - id: AC2\n73\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/readlink -f on a symlink prints the canonical path, matching greadlink.\"\n74\t    traces:\n75\t      - R1.3\n76\t      - R4.2\n77\t  - id: AC3\n78\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/readlink on a non-symlink exits 1, matching greadlink.\"\n79\t    traces:\n80\t      - R1.1\n81\t      - R1.2\n82\t      - R1.4\n83\t      - R3.1\n84\t      - R3.2\n85\t      - R4.1\n86\t  - id: AC4\n87\t    criterion: \"Differential test against greadlink passes for all flag combinations and error cases.\"\n88\t    traces:\n89\t      - R3.1\n90\t      - R3.2\n91\t      - R4.1\n92\t      - R4.2\n93\t      - R4.3\n94\t  - id: AC5\n95\t    criterion: \"cmd/readlink compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n96\t    traces:\n97\t      - R1.1\n98\t      - R1.2\n99\t      - R1.3\n100\t      - R1.4\n101\t      - R1.5\n102\t      - R1.6\n103\t      - R2.1\n104\t      - R2.2\n105\t      - R3.1\n106\t      - R3.2\n107\t      - R4.1\n108\t      - R4.2\n109\t      - R4.3\n110\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0859e498-3be4-4090-9e85-7b2d04cb363a","uuid":"c06ea074-75d1-4601-a454-c543c76512f9","timestamp":"2026-05-15T01:12:21.246Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5237/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd050-readlink.yaml","content":"id: srd050-readlink\ntitle: \"cmd/readlink: Print Symlink Target or Canonical Path\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Scripts that manage symbolic links use readlink to inspect link targets and resolve\n  symlink chains to canonical paths. readlink supports multiple canonicalization modes\n  (-f, -e, -m) that differ in how they handle missing path components. The Go implementation\n  must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (greadlink, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte\n  on stdout and exit code, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Print the target of a symbolic link.\n  - G2: Support canonicalization modes (-f, -e, -m) for resolving full paths.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior and canonicalization\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When invoked with a symlink operand and no flags, must print the immediate target of the symbolic link followed by a newline and exit 0.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: If the operand is not a symbolic link (with no flags), must print nothing to stdout and exit 1.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"-f (--canonicalize) must resolve the full canonical path, following all symlinks. The final component need not exist, but the directory containing it must exist.\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: \"-e (--canonicalize-existing) must resolve the full canonical path. Every component of the path must exist; otherwise exit 1.\"\n      - R1.5:\n          text: \"-m (--canonicalize-missing) must resolve the full canonical path. No component need exist.\"\n      - R1.6:\n          text: \"-n (--no-newline) must suppress the trailing newline when printing a single operand.\"\n\n  R2:\n    title: Multiple operands\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: When multiple operands are given, must print each result on a separate line.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: When multiple operands are given with -n, -n is ignored (newlines are always printed between results).\n\n  R3:\n    title: Error handling\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: If no operand is provided, must print a usage error to stderr and exit 1.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (greadlink) via pkg/testutils.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: symlink target, non-symlink operand, -f with existing and partial paths, -e with existing and missing paths, -m with missing paths, -n flag, multiple operands, and error cases.\"\n      - R4.3:\n          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/readlink does not create or modify symbolic links; use cmd/ln for that.\n  - cmd/readlink does not support --relative-to or --relative-base; use cmd/realpath for relative output.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/readlink on a symlink prints the target, matching greadlink.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n      - R1.6\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/readlink -f on a symlink prints the canonical path, matching greadlink.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.3\n      - R4.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/readlink on a non-symlink exits 1, matching greadlink.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R4.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Differential test against greadlink passes for all flag combinations and error cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"cmd/readlink compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n      - R1.6\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n","numLines":110,"startLine":1,"totalLines":110}}}
