{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running an automated code generation pipeline (\"stitch\" task #5237). The task is to implement srd050-readlink requirements R1.5, R1.6, R2.1, and R2.2 in the existing cmd/readlink package. Specifically:\n   - R1.5: `-m (--canonicalize-missing)` must resolve the full canonical path where no component need exist\n   - R1.6: `-n (--no-newline)` must suppress the trailing newline when printing a single operand\n   - R2.1: When multiple operands are given, must print each result on a separate line\n   - R2.2: When multiple operands are given with -n, -n is ignored (newlines always printed between results)\n   \n   Files to modify: cmd/readlink/main.go and cmd/readlink/readlink_test.go\n   Acceptance criteria: compiles, go vet passes, features work per SRD, tests pass, differential tests match greadlink\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern (comparing Go binary output against GNU reference binary `greadlink`)\n   - pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests and DiffTest struct for test harness\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n   - Canonicalization modes: -f (all but last must exist), -e (all must exist), -m (none need exist)\n   - Path resolution using filepath.Abs, filepath.EvalSymlinks, recursive resolution\n   - Go-unix-utils project conventions (copyright header, no git commands, build to bin/)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd050-readlink.yaml**\n     - Source of truth for requirements. Key requirements for this task:\n       - R1.5: `-m` resolves full canonical path, no component need exist\n       - R1.6: `-n` suppresses trailing newline for single operand\n       - R2.1: Multiple operands print each on separate line\n       - R2.2: `-n` ignored with multiple operands\n     \n   - **cmd/readlink/main.go** (existing, needs modification)\n     - Already implements ALL the logic for R1.5, R1.6, R2.1, R2.2\n     - Package comment says `// Implements srd050-readlink R1.1-R1.4.` - needs updating\n     - Key functions: `canonicalizeM()` handles -m mode, `doCanonM()` recursively resolves\n     - The main loop already handles multiple operands and -n suppression logic:\n       ```go\n       if noNewline && len(operands) == 1 {\n           fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, result)\n       } else {\n           fmt.Fprintln(os.Stdout, result)\n       }\n       ```\n     - Flag parsing already handles 'm' short flag and '--canonicalize-missing' long form\n   \n   - **cmd/readlink/readlink_test.go** (existing, needs modification)\n     - Has tests for R1.1-R1.4 and error cases only\n     - Uses `testutils.BuildBinary`, `exec.LookPath(\"greadlink\")`, normalizers for binary names and error text\n     - Creates temp directory with regular file, symlink, partial path, and missing path fixtures\n     - MISSING test cases for: -m flag, -n flag, multiple operands, multiple operands with -n\n     - Full existing test file shown above (92 lines)\n\n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (reference, not to be modified)\n     - DiffTest struct: `{ Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles }`\n     - RunDiffTests runs each test as named subtest\n     - buildEnv sets LC_ALL=C by default\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - I had just finished reading files and was about to implement changes\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that the implementation code already covers all four requirements (R1.5, R1.6, R2.1, R2.2) from the prior task that implemented R1.1-R1.4\n   - The main work is: update the package comment in main.go and add differential test cases to readlink_test.go\n   - Test cases needed: -m with completely missing paths, -n with single