tures to existing readlink implementation\" and \"Add differential test cases for R1.5, R1.6, R2.1, R2.2\". The existing test fixtures include `missingPath := filepath.Join(tmp, \"nodir\", \"nofile\")` which is perfect for -m testing. New test entries needed in the tests slice follow the existing pattern of `testutils.DiffTest{Name: \"...\", Args: []string{...}, Env: lcEnv}`.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5237/0859e498-3be4-4090-9e85-7b2d04cb363a.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0859e498-3be4-4090-9e85-7b2d04cb363a","uuid":"9756b0e8-77f1-48f6-9adb-e98755636086","timestamp":"2026-05-15T01:13:21.063Z","isSynthetic":true}
